    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-29T04:10:40+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T04:10:40+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T17:40:40Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T17:40:40Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system south of WA extends a ridge over southern parts of the state while a weak trough lies across central Australia near the norther border. The high will drift over the southeast today and into the Tasman Sea on Friday, allowing a trough and low pressure system to move across SA on Friday. A brief high pressure system settles over SA on Saturday before another trough and low starts to move across from WA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-29T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Ceduna, most likely late this afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Ceduna during this afternoon and evening. Winds easterly 25 to 35 km/h turning northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h in the morning. Daytime maximum temperatures around 30.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers east of Ceduna, medium chance elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h shifting west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon and evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower south of Streaky Bay in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then shifting east to southeasterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Streaky Bay. Medium chance of showers south of Streaky Bay, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds easterly 25 to 35 km/h turning north to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h during the morning then tending northeast to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
